span></a><a class="city reveal" href="/service-cities/dayton-ohio/"><img src="/assets/img/photos/tornado-damage.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/tornado-damage-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/tornado-damage.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 50vw, 300px" width="1200" height="900" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="city-b"><b>Dayton</b><small>Montgomery County</small></span></a><a class="city reveal" href="/service-cities/canton-ohio/"><img src="/assets/img/photos/house-porch.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/house-porch-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/house-porch.webp 1024w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 50vw, 300px" width="1024" height="768" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="city-b"><b>Canton</b><small>Stark County</small></span></a><a class="city reveal" href="/service-cities/youngstown-ohio/"><img src="/assets/img/photos/storm-clouds.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/storm-clouds-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/storm-clouds.webp 1024w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 50vw, 300px" width="1024" height="683" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="city-b"><b>Youngstown</b><small>Mahoning County</small></span></a><a class="city reveal" href="/service-cities/sandusky-ohio/"><img src="/assets/img/photos/lake-erie.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/lake-erie-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/lake-erie.webp 1024w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 50vw, 300px" width="1024" height="576" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="city-b"><b>Sandusky</b><small>Erie County</small></span></a><a class="city reveal" href="/service-cities/lima-ohio/"><img src="/assets/img/photos/ohio-farm.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/ohio-farm-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/ohio-farm.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 50vw, 300px" width="1200" height="900" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="city-b"><b>Lima</b><small>Allen County</small></span></a><a class="city reveal" href="/service-cities/xenia-ohio/"><img src="/assets/img/photos/tornado-aerial.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/tornado-aerial-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/tornado-aerial.webp 1024w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 50vw, 300px" width="1024" height="576" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="city-b"><b>Xenia</b><small>Greene County</small></span></a><a class="city reveal" href="/service-cities/zanesville-ohio/"><img src="/assets/img/photos/ice-storm.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/ice-storm-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/ice-storm.webp 1024w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 50vw, 300px" width="1024" height="768" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="city-b"><b>Zanesville</b><small>Muskingum County</small></span></a></div></div></section>
<section class="sec sec-tint"><div class="wrap"><div class="sec-head reveal"><p class="kicker">Regions</p><h2>How claims differ across Ohio</h2><p>The same policy wording plays out very differently on a snowbelt farmhouse, a Columbus subdivision and a Cincinnati hillside home.</p></div><div class="region-grid" data-stagger><article class="region reveal"><div class="region-ph"><img src="/assets/img/photos/lake-erie.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/lake-erie-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/lake-erie.webp 1024w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 380px" width="1024" height="576" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div><div class="region-b"><p class="region-k">Cleveland · Akron · Canton · Youngstown</p><h2 class="card-h">Northeast Ohio</h2><p>Lake-effect snow piles up in the snowbelt east of Cleveland, which means ice dams, snow-load damage and burst pipes in century-old homes. Spring and summer bring hail and straight-line wind across Summit, Stark and Mahoning counties.</p><ul class="chips"><li>Lake-effect snow</li><li>Ice dams</li><li>Hail</li><li>Old slate roofs</li></ul></div></article><article class="region reveal"><div class="region-ph"><img src="/assets/img/photos/ohio-farm.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/ohio-farm-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/ohio-farm.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 380px" width="1200" height="900" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div><div class="region-b"><p class="region-k">Toledo · Sandusky · Lima</p><h2 class="card-h">Northwest Ohio</h2><p>Flat farmland gives storms a clear run. Tornadoes, derecho winds and hail cross Lucas, Wood, Erie and Allen counties, while Lake Erie adds wind-driven rain and lakeshore exposure.</p><ul class="chips"><li>Tornadoes</li><li>Straight-line wind</li><li>Hail</li><li>Farm buildings</li></ul></div></article><article class="region reveal"><div class="region-ph"><img src="/assets/img/photos/columbus-skyline.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/columbus-skyline-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/columbus-skyline.webp 1024w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 380px" width="1024" height="657" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div><div class="region-b"><p class="region-k">Columbus and suburbs</p><h2 class="card-h">Central Ohio</h2><p>Franklin County’s fast-growing suburbs mean big subdivisions of similar homes — and big hail and wind events that hit thousands of roofs at once, as the 2012 derecho showed.</p><ul class="chips"><li>Derechos</li><li>Hail</li><li>Wind</li><li>Basement water</li></ul></div></article><article class="region reveal"><div class="region-ph"><img src="/assets/img/photos/cincinnati-skyline.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/cincinnati-skyline-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/cincinnati-skyline.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 380px" width="1200" height="800" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div><div class="region-b"><p class="region-k">Cincinnati · Dayton · Xenia</p><h2 class="card-h">Southwest Ohio</h2><p>The Miami Valley sits in one of Ohio’s busiest tornado corridors, from Xenia in 1974 to the Memorial Day 2019 outbreak. Cincinnati’s hillside homes add tree, wind and water problems.</p><ul class="chips"><li>Tornadoes</li><li>Hail</li><li>Hillside water</li><li>Tree damage</li></ul></div></article><article class="region reveal"><div class="region-ph"><img src="/assets/img/photos/ice-storm.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/ice-storm-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/ice-storm.webp 1024w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 380px" width="1024" height="768" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div><div class="region-b"><p class="region-k">Zanesville · Athens · Marietta</p><h2 class="card-h">Southeast Ohio</h2><p>Appalachian hills, river towns and older frame and brick homes. Ice storms, fallen trees and basement water are the claims that come up most along the Muskingum and the Ohio River.</p><ul class="chips"><li>Ice storms</li><li>Fallen trees</li><li>River-town basements</li><li>Older homes</li></ul></div></article></div></div></section>
